# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizer builds (docs/port/SANITIZE.md 4): check:function, each
# with its reason. A finding not listed fails its test (halt_on_error=1 in ctest's environment).

# The game C's design: Tracker.idx is declared with 17 slots and the records carry 20, which the N64 code fills
# (pathcommon_sync/group.c's own comment). A member array used past its end, as -Warray-bounds sees 260 times; the
# writes stay inside gCheckpoints at its N64 layout.
bounds:^SyncCheckpointsToPaths$

# The pause menu's rows (the retail pause paths): animControls tests (conflict && !gConflict[p][action]) ||
# action >= 10, so with action 10 it reads the next row's first flag (an arena in the RDRAM window, at its N64
# layout, as the N64 reads it), and the || makes the result true whatever it read.
bounds:^animControls$

# The high scores' name entry (the retail cartridge's records, a race finished: docs/port/QA.md "Integration QA"):
# finishing a name with nothing typed (END pressed first, or its time running out) trims trailing spaces with
# name[len - 1] at len 0, the byte before the name. For player 1 that is humans[7]'s (humans, s16[8], at its N64
# layout), which nothing writes (four humans at most), for the others the previous name's terminator: 0 on the N64
# and here, not a space, so the loop stops before it writes. The retail function's own read, kept.
bounds:^ControlName$

# A blank cartridge only (--no-rom, app_firstrun): with every file empty no heap block fits, and the N64 code reads
# the null block's size too.
null:^AllocateMemory$

# The synthetic cartridge's data (docs/port/SYNTH.md 4): its camera and particle positions are NaN, and the view and
# particle code converts them to integers. None of these on the retail paths (SANITIZE.md 3).
float-cast-overflow:^zoid_draw_window$
float-cast-overflow:^mtx_rotation_to_fixed$
float-cast-overflow:^build_node_matrix$
float-cast-overflow:^build_node_matrix_rows4$
float-cast-overflow:^tan_cody_waite$
float-cast-overflow:^zoid_draw_object$
float-cast-overflow:^ShotToWorldCollision$
float-cast-overflow:^video_build_adjusted_mode$

